---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ReviewNotice from '../components/ReviewNotice.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/images/about-founder-portrait.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Us" description="The story of Global Sushi Academy and its founder, Ram Kaji Gosai.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)]">About Us</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-4xl">Ram Kaji Gosai</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">Founder, Global Sushi Academy</p>

    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt="Ram Kaji Gosai, founder of Global Sushi Academy, in chef's whites holding a wooden boat-shaped sushi platter."
      width={480}
      class="mt-8 w-full max-w-sm object-cover sm:float-right sm:ml-8"
    />

    <div class="mt-8">
      <ReviewNotice
        notes={[
          "Bio text is carried over from the legacy website's database, written before the 2026 rebrand — please check it still reads the way you want it to, and that every detail (years, places, names) is still accurate.",
          "The source text named the 2015 course as \"Volkschule Bad Schwartau\" — likely means the Volkshochschule (adult education center), but left as just \"a course in Bad Schwartau\" below rather than guessing. Please confirm the institution's actual name.",
          "Portrait reused from the legacy site. It shows Ram himself, so there's no third-party consent question, but the banner visible behind him in the shot carries the old logo and the old domain — worth a tighter crop, a different photo, or a fresh one before this goes live.",
          "Manna Sushi & Grill section added per your instruction (same owner, same address, confirmed via manna-restaurants.de). Kept deliberately short. Catering and take-away are no longer offered, so they are not mentioned anywhere on the site.",
        ]}
      />
    </div>

    <div class="markdown-body mt-10">
      <p>
        Global Sushi Academy is a premier sushi school in Europe, based in Germany. Ram Kaji
        Gosai started Global Sushi Academy with the aim of helping people realize their dreams
        of becoming a top sushi chef — and to promote sushi and other Asian dishes as delicious,
        healthy food throughout the world.
      </p>

      <h2>Ram's story</h2>

      <p>
        Ram Kaji Gosai was born in Bhaktapur, Nepal — the birthplace of Buddha and home to the
        tallest mountain in the world, Mt. Everest.
      </p>

      <p>
        At the age of 18, Ram started his culinary journey working at a small restaurant. He
        worked there for three years, learning both Western and Japanese cuisines.
      </p>

      <p>
        In 1999, Ram started his own restaurant in Nepal and got an early taste of
        entrepreneurship. He ran it for three years before, driven by big dreams and high
        ambitions, moving to Europe in 2002.
      </p>

      <p>
        A hard-working and determined person, Ram gained extensive experience across Europe,
        working with top Japanese and Nepalese sushi masters in the Netherlands, Spain, Portugal
        and Norway, and at major hotels including Ostsee Scharbeutz in Schleswig-Holstein,
        Germany.
      </p>

      <p>
        In 2015, Ram took a sushi course in Bad Schwartau, Germany, and completed a private
        Advanced Sushi Chef course in Los Angeles, USA, under the renowned Japanese sushi master
        Andy Matsuda.
      </p>

      <p>
        After many years working in top restaurants and hotels, Ram returned to his
        entrepreneurial ambitions and set out to help others learn the art of sushi making. In
        July 2016, he opened Global Sushi Academy — a sushi school dedicated to training the
        next generation of sushi chefs.
      </p>

      <p>
        Through Global Sushi Academy, Ram's mission is to train enthusiastic, dedicated students
        to a professional standard and to promote healthy Japanese cuisine around the globe.
      </p>

      <h2>Manna Sushi &amp; Grill</h2>

      <p>
        Ram also owns and runs <a href="https://manna-restaurants.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manna Sushi &amp; Grill</a>,
        a Japanese and Nepalese restaurant at the academy's own address, Marienkirchhof 2–3 in
        Lübeck.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
